  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes typecheck. I couldn't run it in a browser or run `vite build`, so the visuals and the facing direction are untested.\n\n- **Soldier:** `/assets/soldier.glb` loads through `defineModelAssets`, scaled to 1.8 m, and plays `Walk` in a loop. I took the sha256 from the soldier example in `docs/agents/recipes.md` rather than computing it from the file.\n- **Path:** each frame the soldier is placed on a radius-4 circle around the origin. Its yaw is `atan2(vx, vz)` of the travel direction. This assumes the model faces +Z, so if it walks sideways or backwards, change `MODEL_YAW_OFFSET`.\n- **Controls:** `r` calls `play(\"Run\", { crossFade: 0.4 })` and `w` switches back to `Walk` the same way. Ground speed eases between 1.4 m/s and 3.6 m/s instead of jumping.\n- **Scene:** a ground plane, a darker track plane under the circle, and neutral, hemisphere and shadow-casting directional lights. A fixed perspective camera at (0, 8.5, 9.5) looks at the origin and frames the whole circle.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the first animation frame after `app.ready()` resolves, so it only fires once the model has loaded. I avoided top-level `await` so the default Vite build target doesn't reject it.",
